Tengo un plataformas 2D en Godot 4.3. Mi `player.gd` (CharacterBody2D) ya tiene unas 600 líneas y todo está en `_physics_process` con un montón de `if/elif` y booleanos: `is_jumping`, `is_dashing`, `is_attacking`, `is_wall_sliding`, `is_hurt`, `can_dash`. Estados: idle, run, jump, fall, dash, wall-slide, attack, hurt. Cada vez que añado algo (ahora quiero un double jump) se rompe otra cosa; por ejemplo, si me golpean durante el dash me quedo atascado en dash. Te pego un trozo:

```gdscript
func _physics_process(delta):
    if is_hurt:
        hurt_timer -= delta
        if hurt_timer <= 0: is_hurt = false
        velocity.x = knockback.x
    elif is_dashing:
        dash_timer -= delta
        velocity = dash_dir * DASH_SPEED
        if dash_timer <= 0: is_dashing = false
    elif is_attacking:
        velocity.x = 0
    else:
        if Input.is_action_just_pressed("jump") and (is_on_floor() or is_wall_sliding):
            velocity.y = JUMP_VELOCITY
            is_jumping = true
        if Input.is_action_just_pressed("dash") and can_dash:
            is_dashing = true; can_dash = false; dash_timer = DASH_TIME
        # ... 500 líneas más
    move_and_slide()
```

¿Qué patrón de diseño debería usar para ordenar esto y cómo lo migro sin romper el juego? Dame la estructura concreta.

Can you review this PR before I merge it? It's for our Node/TypeScript order service. Today we only send emails through SendGrid; product says SMS is 'maybe next year'. `IOrderRepository` has a single `PostgresOrderRepository` implementation and is replaced by an in-memory fake in our unit tests.

```ts
// config.ts
export class Config {
  private static instance: Config;
  private constructor(public readonly values: Record<string, string>) {}
  static getInstance(): Config {
    if (!Config.instance) Config.instance = new Config({ ...process.env } as Record<string, string>);
    return Config.instance;
  }
}

// notifications/INotificationSender.ts
export interface INotificationSender {
  send(to: string, subject: string, body: string): Promise<void>;
}

// notifications/AbstractNotificationSenderFactory.ts
export abstract class AbstractNotificationSenderFactory {
  abstract createSender(): INotificationSender;
}
export class EmailNotificationSenderFactory extends AbstractNotificationSenderFactory {
  createSender(): INotificationSender {
    return new SendGridEmailSender(Config.getInstance().values.SENDGRID_KEY);
  }
}

// notifications/NotificationSenderFactoryProvider.ts
export class NotificationSenderFactoryProvider {
  static getFactory(kind: 'email'): AbstractNotificationSenderFactory {
    switch (kind) {
      case 'email': return new EmailNotificationSenderFactory();
    }
  }
}

// events/EventBus.ts
type Handler = (payload: unknown) => void;
export const EventBus = {
  handlers: new Map<string, Handler[]>(),
  on(event: string, handler: Handler) { /* push into map */ },
  emit(event: string, payload: unknown) { this.handlers.get(event)?.forEach(h => h(payload)); },
};

// orders/OrderService.ts
export class OrderService {
  constructor(private repo: IOrderRepository) {}
  async placeOrder(order: Order) {
    await this.repo.save(order);
    EventBus.emit('order.placed', order);
  }
}

// orders/handlers.ts
EventBus.on('order.placed', async (o: any) => {
  const sender = NotificationSenderFactoryProvider.getFactory('email').createSender();
  await sender.send(o.customerEmail, 'Order confirmed', `Order ${o.id}`);
});
